4|0@dbz^1440132799#cuack9x:Dullahan3470$:Gohan wasn't a fighter like his father, but at the same time he still trained to protect the things he cared about. I just want a pay off to the arc. It felt like the entire Buu saga already revolved around Gohan being lax in his training --&gt; Gohan realizes that he needs to be stronger to protect the world --&gt; Gohan powers up. They even had the classic Goku/Vegta poses when Gohan showed up on Earth. Or you know, atleast put him into a Piccolo role. Let him be a mentor, let him be a strategizer, let him do something. As it is, pretty much all the characters that aren't Goku and Vegeta are completely fucking irrelevant. They're too weak to be useful. This is boring. Remember fucking Namek? Where we got to see Krillin and Kid Gohan being useful, helping fight Frieza even though he far outstripped them in power? When we got to see Piccolo and Vegeta kick ass even though they were again outclassed? Remember in the Cell saga where Piccolo was strong enough to intimidate Imperfect Cell? Or even in the Buu saga where we had Gohan and Gotenks as capable of atleast putting up a decent fight. The series stopped being about fighters teaming up against insurmountable odds and started to be all about Goku and Vegeta trying to outlevel each other. Whis even says "If you two worked together, you'd be unstoppable." Resurrection of F was completely devoid of tension, unlike the original Frieza Saga, largely because of this focus on simply being more powerful rather than outsmarting your opponent or having a dramatic transformation. Instead we got offscreen bullshit. So now we have this entire cast of characters that are being dragged along in the story, but are too weak to be relevant as fighters. To the point where they fought against severely nerfed Frieza henchmen that were probably on par with fucking Raditz at best. And at the top of the pile is Gohan, who already went through this fucking character arc in the Buu saga where he realized that neglecting his training was a mistake. It's like EVERYONE FUCKING FORGOT that the next generation needs to be able to take over for Goku and Vegeta when they eventually die. And don't even get me started on how boring of a character Videl became after she got hitched. 
