6|0@dbz^1440130249#cuabhyg:SonofNamek$:It has nothing to do w/ him becoming the lead. People want him to be consistent. Like, he doesn't need to be a fighter akin to Goku/Vegeta. But he shouldn't be some goofy dork. The role is reserved for Goku and Goten. In that sense, Toriyama tried too much to make Gohan into Goku 2.0 when he should be Gohan. By doing that, he killed off the character of Gohan. In all honesty, this is just Toriyama being a poor 'serious writer'....something he has admitted openly. As for the character itself? Gohan has always been a traumatized, quiet, sensitive kid at heart who gets deeply upset at injustice. He's an idealist. If we had to make Gohan consistent, he'd be traumatized by his father's death as a child, being kidnapped/trained by Piccolo, and seeing his friends die on the battlefield. He'd have mild-PTSD (not stated) and would want to be left alone more. He'd be much closer in personality to Future Gohan. Thus, more reclusive and solo. Silent but tough. Though, he'll still be prone to cracking a joke once in a while. And he's not a leader like Goku or Vegeta but more of a reliable/dependable guy. In that sense, he'd be like Piccolo.....the guy who raised him. And he shouldn't become a fighter (father) or a scholar (mother). He should differ by becoming be an artist. It suits his personality more.
