1|0@dbz^1440135676#cuadn9y:chocobo606$:Gohan was smart, went to school, will be a professor, found a great girlfriend who is going to become his wife, and have a child. He may be a hybrid, but all he's ever wanted was to be human. Yes, he was also trained by his father and Piccolo, went through some of the toughest battles against the toughest enemies and in the end was one of the strongest fighters ever...but only because he had to be, not because he wanted to be. I love THAT Gohan. I don't love the Gohan everyone worships, because he is, in my opinion, a horrible fighter, and isn't capable of winning a challenging fight. His fights consisted of vastly overpowering his enemy when he did win. And lastly...it's not like Gohan can't find a way to unlock his hidden potential again at some point in Super. He fell off and became weaker, yes, but that also means he can get it all back because he once again has to.
