1|0@dbz^1440135983#cuadr7z:willy1inch$:I've read the original intention was for Goku to actually stay dead beyond the cell saga, and for gohan to take over as the most powerful saiyan. I agree with the comment that as kids growing up we saw ourselves in gohan, so when he grew up to be incapable, it kind of made us feel betrayed. Because we didn't want to grow up to be lame and tame. I don't think anybody is really asking for gohan to be in the ranks of vegeta and Goku at this point, but we really want to feel like he at least matters. We all know dabura ain't shit, and to see gohan struggle with him is frustrating. In response to the jumpsuit argument, Goku really doesn't look weaker in his. We all want gohan to be a good father and husband, but we still want him to use the gift he was given. They have to write in a sub-cast of villains for him, which is something better left for the tiens, krillins and piccolos. Dragon ball is a fighting show. So when you have a character who is the greatest ever at one point, basically intentionally throw it away, it leaves you with a sour taste.
