0|0@dbz^1440160137#cuakmxn:Dxpoo$:I personally hated Kid Gohan because he cried every damn episode in the Saiyan Saga. As he grew up I really didn't mind him. 
1|0@dbz^1440151633#cuahz7u:ThrowAZilla$:Just dropping by to say I do not hate Gohan. I hate the last minute decision to make him a "push over". I freaking love Gohan! It's just not fair what the writers did to him, after everything up to Cell. 
1|0@dbz^1440196235#cub740k:boscha196$:I can't speak for all the fans but I do not hate Gohan and I don't hate that he he isn't interested in fighting/training but is more interested in studying and family. In fact it is one of the best things about him because as you say it makes him different. All that said, the way he was written in BOG and especially F was lazy. I don't want him to be the strongest character, far from it, but at least acknowledge what he has been through, like the Old Kai power up. "I can still become a Super Saiyan...I think." Yeah...Ok remind me why you need to again? Because you shouldn't, unless your power really dropped that much...which if it did give me some sort of explanation other than "not keeping up with your training." If he went from stronger than Super Saiyan 3 to weaker than Super Saiyan...that makes the power he lost between Cell and Buu look like nothing. And we are supposed to believe he lost all this in what a year instead of 7? Because in BOG he still displayed the ultimate powers and Super Saiyan was just an aesthetic...which I can go re-read the manga 1,000 times and still think he shouldn't even be able to go Super Saiyan. They are just disregarding it. But whatever, Super Saiyan just not giving him a power up is ok too I guess. If the writers and Toriyama decided to pay attention to Gohan in the Buu arc you world essentially have the same character with the same personality but still able to be relevant. Like fighting final, pre golden Freeza before Goku and Vegeta arrive. Maybe he is even losing but it something. That is all I would ask for. Let's be honest the series could use a bridge between Goku/Vegeta and EVERYONE else. I'm hopeful, fingers crossed, that Super handles Gohan differently.
1|0@dbz^1440167447#cuaoewu:UCXC_2015$:I think its because when Gohan beats Cell, he is basically the strongest fighter in the series. Then when we see him again as a young adult, we expect him to be stronger and more badass. But instead we see him actually somewhat weaker and kinda lame. Then when we think we are gonna get redemption and see him kick Buu's ass and builds up to this epic fight, he gets absorbed.
0|0@dbz^1440172076#cuaremo:anonpurpose$:People want him to be like he was fighting Cell or fighting Bojack. The unstoppable, cut your stooges in half with my blows, badass. They just want to see more moments like this, and I admit it would be cool, but that's not what the creator wants. It also wouldn't make a lot of sense story wise at this point. They would have to need a 3rd SSG for some reason. I can't see how Toriyama would get the story to that point and it feels like it'd be lazy writing just to give the fans what they want. Isn't that what people complain about already? Toriyama supposedly bent to the will of fans to make Goku the hero again. So they want him to do that for them, and make Gohan the hero. Toriyama thought Gohan wasn't that type of person. He isn't the main hero because that's not what he wants to focus on. The creator's vision wins. People will always keep disagreeing no matter where the story or characters go. It's nice that this series can actually elicit such strong emotions. 
1|0@dbz^1440694775#cuhmwjv:nightwing612$:Problem with Gohan is that he was supposed to have fixed his problems. He can be a pacifist all he wants or an arrogant uberman but he should have learned that these quirks is what killed Android 16 and Goku during the Cell Saga AND YET, he spent 7 years hardly doing any training?! AT THIS POINT, HE WAS THE EARTH'S ONLY HOPE!! HE SHOULD HAVE BEEN AWARE THAT HE NEEDS TO TRAIN BECAUSE EARTH'S FATE IS ON HIS SHOULDERS Now whatever happened, Old Kai was supposed to have unlocked all his potential and put him back at the top of the power rankings. BUT HE ENDED UP BEING ARROGANT AGAIN (JUST LIKE DURING THE CELL SAGA) AND DIDN'T BEAT SUPER BUU WHEN HE COULD NOW AFTER ALL THAT. HE SKIPS HIS TRAINING GETS ONESHOTTED BY BOTH BEERUS AND GOLDEN FRIEZA (NOT TO MENTION APPARENTLY LOSING HIS MYSTIC FORM??!!) Sigh. It is so hard to be a Gohan fan nowadays
